{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/259834-geist-chronicles-integirty-synergy-and-conflict-of-minds","id":259834,"title":"Geist Chronicles: Integirty, Synergy and Conflict of Minds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-18T10:24:50-07:00","id":259834,"title":"Geist Chronicles: Integirty, Synergy and Conflict of Minds","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">MugaSofa has asked me to start posting work from my sadly unfinished Geist Chronicles book (which could arguably be the Krewe Chronicles, or Geist 2.0 I suppose) So to start with I present the rules for Integrity, Synergy and Conflict of Minds. If this thread gets interest there will be more to follow.<br /> <br /> These three are what I consider the thematic core of the game. That's not to say I think they'll dominate the play-time, rather I think of them like feeding in Vampire. You may not run many feeding scenes, but the need for blood defines vampire society. In Geist terms they represent why a couch potato who comes back is going to get off that sofa and size his second chance by the throat - he has to invest in his attributes to defend himself against the Geist. He has to go out and indulge his Geist's Passions. He has to found a Krewe and live by it's mythology. Or he has to unearth his Geist's Past.<br /> <br /> Because if he doesn't do at least one of those, the Geist is going to take the body for joyrides. Now this dosn't automatically require interacting with the dead, but it easily can with the right Passions, Krewe Mythology or if Ghosts are the best witnesses to an event deep in the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> So without further adu: </span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Modified Traits: Integrity and Synergy</span></b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A person is bound to a Geist. There are two minds and so there are two traits that affect the Sin-Eater\u2019s mental fortitude: Integrity and Synergy. The Geist\u2019s own mind is too inflexible to be represented by a 1-10 scale. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Integrity</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Integrity measures the mental state of the human Sin-Eater, in this it remains mostly unchanged. The Bound have died and returned with a Geist glued to their mind and soul, that\u2019s a pretty extreme situation and it can change a person, but it is a change caused by trauma and circumstance. The Sin-Eater\u2019s mind and morality have not been metaphysically altered by their reincarnation. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mechanically Integrity is unchanged, however when an effect depends on a character's Integrity rating Sin-Eaters use Integrity + Synergy (maximum of 10) unless stated otherwise. The actual array of Breaking Points is different. Sin-Eaters are not nearly as shocked by the supernatural as a typical mortal and Some Sin-Eaters can kill without suffering a Breaking Point, others are quite proud of the fact they retain the usual instinctive revulsion at the thought of ending someone\u2019s life. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Synergy</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Synergy measures the working relationship between the Sin-Eater and the Gesit. At high Synergy the pair could each control half of the body, acting in perfect unison, more importantly both consider themselves to be on some level parts of the same person. It is hard to maintain a strong sense of self, a firm Integrity, at high synergy. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A more modest Synergy would represent a solid working relationship where both get time to pursue their own interests and avoid pushing each others buttons or a pair who are lucky enough to have common interests. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A partnership with low or no Synergy usually means that the Sin-Eater is in charge - it was originally their body, they have the home-turf advantage - but punctuated with frequent clashes over control. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mechanically Synergy increases a Sin-Eater\u2019s maximum Support pool, each dot in Synergy allows one extra point of Support. Synergy is also added to certain dice pools, most noticeably Conflict of Minds in which Synergy provides a bonus when the Sin-Eater initiates a conflict but a penalty when the Geist initiates.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sidebar: Rumours on the Twilight Network </span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">First Krewe I ever ran with, we had this guy with a hundred romans in his head. Believe it! He started turning Roman himself, wearing armour and talking in latin. So the other day I saw a fresh, same Geist only my brv was one of the romans. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Trebuchet MS\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Support</span></b></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">All Sin-Eaters have a pool of Support equal to 3 + Synergy. Support is an abstract value which can represent many different things: It could represent your Geist feeling gratitude or liking it\u2019s partner. It could represent your Geist being willing to put aside it\u2019s own needs when the pair are in danger. It could even represent your Geist being afraid of your Sin-Eater, maybe she\u2019s threatened one of the Geist\u2019s Anchors. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Spending Support </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The player can spend one point of Support as a reflexive action to automatically win any Conflict of Minds roll. The player decides whether this represents the Sin-Eater defeating the Geist or if the Conflict of Minds never happened. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Regaining Support</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You regain one point of Support if the Sin-Eater helps the Geist indulge it\u2019s Passion or indulges that Passion on behalf of the Geist. </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Sin-Eater may opt to automatically fail a Conflict of Minds roll in exchange for one point of Support. </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If you uncover a new and significant piece of information about your Geist\u2019s Past, refill your Support pool completely (Geists tend to forget about their human life in between partners). </span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If you resolve one of your Geist\u2019s Anchors refill your Support pool completely. </span></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sidebar: Morbid Passions</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Some Geist\u2019s have Passions so abhorrent that their partner would never willingly allow them to indulge. A player can opt to declare their Geist\u2019s passions Morbid as an out of game declaration. If they do so the Sin-Eater can never regain Support from indulging their Geist\u2019s Passion. As a consolation prize they gain a Beat every time the Geist initiates a Conflict of Minds while their Support pool is empty. (This is in addition to the usual Beat for losing a Conflict of Minds) </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Morbid Passions do not have to involve eating babies. Anything that the Sin-Eater personally finds repulsive could qualify, even if a hypothetical average person would consider it perfectly normal. It is recommended though, that Morbid Passions are only invoked when there is little chance of the Sin-Eater changing her mind. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In essence this rule exists for players to declare as a matter of narrative intent that they are interested in a story about their character fighting their Geist. As a corollary the group should be forthright in saying no if the story is supposed to be about exploring the Underworld and doesn't want the plot to get waylaid by a rabid Geist. Role playing is a communal activity, it is important that everyone is on the same page before play starts. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Conflict of Minds</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sidebar: A Convenient Reference</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Here\u2019s the base dice pool for a Conflict of Minds.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Torn: Strength + Stamina</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Silent: Resolve + Stamina</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stricken: Manipulation + Composure</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Prey: Intelligence + Wits</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Forgotten: Wits + Composure</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Geists are not loyal lapdogs who dispense advice and provide occult power. They have their own goals and Passions. If the Geist feels that they aren\u2019t getting enough out of the relationship or that the Sin-Eater is making a really bad decision they may try to seize control themselves. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Torn attack their partner to take control. For the Silent, sometimes they just can\u2019t endure any longer and when they give in the Geist is left in charge. Stricken Geists favour persuasion and trickery. The Prey cannot be opposed, Sin-Eaters must anticipate their desires and give them no reason to insist. Finally The Forgotten are varied and random. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Yet for all this diversity a Conflict of Minds is simple. When your Geist attempts to take over roll your base Conflict of Minds pool - Synergy with any situational modifiers.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dramatic Failure: The Geist takes over for a scene, it\u2019s control is so absolute that the Sin-Eater blacks out for part or all of the scene. Take the Dude, Where\u2019s my Body condition. Also: take a Beat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Failure: The Geist takes over for a scene, leaving the Sin-Eater as just a voice in their own head. This is usually less traumatic than it sounds, something about being bound at the soul helps ease the experience. It\u2019s not enough to make watching yourself go on a murder spree palatable, but it helps. Also: take a Beat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Success: The Sin-Eater remains in control, the Geist may not initiate any further Clashes of Wills this scene. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exceptional Success: The Sin-Eater remains in control, the Geist may not initiate any further Clashes of Wills this scene. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Before rolling the player may choose to spend a point of Support instead. The player decides if this represents defeating their Geist or retroactively declaring that the Conflict of Minds never happened. Either way, spending a point of Support mechanically counts as a Success. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sin-Eaters can also initiate Clashes of Wills. Any time the player wishes the Geist to act in a certain way and it does not want to the Sin-Eater can declare a Conflict of Minds. Roll your base Conflict of Minds pool + Synergy with any situational modifiers. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dramatic Failure: The Sin-Eater erroneously believes that the Geist will behave and lets it loose. Roleplay the result. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Failure: The Geist\u2019s mood remains unchanged. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Success: The Geist is persuaded or threatened into playing along. It will do what the Sin-Eater wants. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exceptional Success: The Geist and Sin-Eater come to an accord and act as one. Take the Teamwork! condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As always, a point of Support can be spent in place of rolling for a single automatic success. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A common motivation for Sin-Eaters to invoke a Conflict of Minds is if they want to Manifest their Geist to fight off some threat. When the Sin-Eater invokes a Conflict of Minds while in danger the results are different. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dramatic Failure or Failure: The Geist is willing to help defend the Sin-Eater, but it will do so it\u2019s way. It might carry the Sin-Eater away from the battle or ignore pleas to fight non-lethally. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Success: The Geist is persuaded or threatened into playing along. It will do what the Sin-Eater wants. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exceptional Success: The Geist and Sin-Eater come to an accord and act as one. Take the Teamwork! condition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As always, a point of Support can be spent in place of rolling for a single automatic success. </span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-18-2014, 02:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T11:45:57-07:00","id":259894,"title":"","content":"fantastic, it didn't make much sense that when they wrote Geist they didn't much emphasis on the relationship between the sin-eater and their geister. anyhow i like it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T06:14:43-07:00","id":260565,"title":"","content":"I think it goes without saying that I like it so far. The only real addition to this is a conflict of minds roll that strongly favors the Sin-eater (it wouldn't be Geist if they were able to just outright take control all the time)<br /> <br /> I'd like to see some examples of what the Geists can do that the Sin-eaters cant directly do themselves, seeing as they can reverse possess their Geists to interact with twilight. I kind of like the idea that the relationship actually goes two ways: there are some things that SE's can do that Geists need them for, their are some things that Geists can do that SE's need them for, and there are some things they mutually get because of their partnership (like plasma fortification)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T05:09:16-07:00","id":262020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/259834-geist-chronicles-integirty-synergy-and-conflict-of-minds#post259834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity measures the mental state of the human Sin-Eater, in this it remains mostly unchanged. The Bound have died and returned with a Geist glued to their mind and soul, that\u2019s a pretty extreme situation and it can change a person, but it is a change caused by trauma and circumstance. The Sin-Eater\u2019s mind and morality have not been metaphysically altered by their reincarnation. ... Synergy measures the working relationship between the Sin-Eater and the Gesit. At high Synergy the pair could each control half of the body, acting in perfect unison, more importantly both consider themselves to be on some level parts of the same person. It is hard to maintain a strong sense of self, a firm Integrity, at high synergy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I quite like this distinction. It might be worth making increasing one trait via experience be a breaking point for the other - increasing your union with your Geist necessarily threatens your individual sense of self, while nurturing your individuality poses a risk of the Geist feeling its needs are neglected. (Should an increase be granted purely through roleplaying, this doesn't apply - we can assume that what the breaking point represents has already been played out).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Geist\u2019s have Passions so abhorrent that their partner would never willingly allow them to indulge. A player can opt to declare their Geist\u2019s passions Morbid as an out of game declaration. If they do so the Sin-Eater can never regain Support from indulging their Geist\u2019s Passion. </div> </div> </div>Why would the Geist not offer support for this regardless? What about instead making indulging this passion be an automatic breaking point for Integrity, or even an automatic loss of Integrity? That would allow for passions that aren't just evil, but also insane or just plain alien. It also means the Sin-Eater <i>can</i> change her mind and indulge the passion, it's just going to scar the mortal side of her psyche.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here\u2019s the base dice pool for a Conflict of Minds.<br /> Torn: Strength + Stamina </div> </div> </div>Even for the Torn, I don't think this should be a purely physical pool. I'd suggest replacing Strength with Presence, which is still evocative of force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T05:41:12-07:00","id":262064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/259834-geist-chronicles-integirty-synergy-and-conflict-of-minds?p=262020#post262020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I quite like this distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wouldn't make it an automatic Breaking Point; because you might progress from Integrity to Synergy at seperate times.<br /> <br /> Let me explain with an example. Jerome comes back as a Torn, and the mortuary worker who witnesses this is a Hunter. She calls her Cell then tries to stab him; Jerome uses his powers in self defense and kills her, this costs him a point of Integrity.<br /> <br /> A few hours later the Cell turns up at his home. While they're breaking down the door Jerome's Geist starts giving him advice on strategy, his powers, and how to survive. Jerome kills the hunters, and the player says that since he's already lost Integrtiy from the mortuary worker - he feels Jerome's already become hardened to self-defensive killing. He'd just returned, his mind was in a mallable state, etc. However Jerome's player does want to buy a point of Synergy because of how Jerome and his Geist teamed up.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want that point of Synergy to trigger a Breaking Point, because it fits so well with the earlier breaking point.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I might do is have a rule that you can't have more than ten points combined in Integrity or Synergy - actually, I wonder where that rule went. I thought it was there already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/259834-geist-chronicles-integirty-synergy-and-conflict-of-minds?p=262020#post262020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the Geist not offer support for this regardless?</div> </div> </div> </div> Support exists as an abstract out-of-game concept. Morbid Passions is also an out-of-game concept. So the two fit togeather better Morbid Passions would with Integrity; as Integrity is an in-game concept.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want it to be an automatic Integrity loss; because when you're having a long term conflict with the Geist; Integrity is your &quot;score&quot;. That mans in situations where you slip up and your Geist takes over and indulges it's Passion; it's more important that your charachter gets their roll to resist Integirty loss than it would be if your conflict with the Geist is a minor plot compared to your conflict with that other Krewe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/259834-geist-chronicles-integirty-synergy-and-conflict-of-minds?p=262020#post262020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even for the Torn, I don't think this should be a purely physical pool. I'd suggest replacing Strength with Presence, which is still evocative of force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually. That's a pretty good idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of which. It's probably about time for the next thread. Coming up: Krewes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T13:04:26-07:00","id":266389,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">My one issue with this system is that it feels a little too ... <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">competitive</span></span>. It's purely a contest of strength.<br /> <br /> The rules themselves are fine; it just needs more representation for threats and favors and bargains. In a word, <i>co-operation</i>. (So, expanded Support rules?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/259834-geist-chronicles-integirty-synergy-and-conflict-of-minds?p=262064#post262064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I might do is have a rule that you can't have more than ten points combined in Integrity or Synergy - actually, I wonder where that rule went. I thought it was there already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you're worried this might not have the same &quot;feel&quot;, but why not treat it as a single scale, like Harmony? (This is the same as having one equal 10 minus the other; you're only really measuring their <i>relative</i> strength.)<br /> <br /> Say, Synergy-7 is a strong Geist, Synergy-3 is a strong Sin-Eater. At Synergy-0 your Geist might abandon you; but at Synergy 10 you're little more than a puppet. Ideally, you want give and take - somewhere in the middle.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-26-2014, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T13:09:49-07:00","id":266392,"title":"","content":"Because low Integrity and low Synergy is an entirely seperate thing to low Integrity and High Synergy. Threats, favours and bargens could be represented with conditions that give you support if you voluntarily take them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T10:46:19-07:00","id":267522,"title":"","content":"I see the opposite... That High Synergy is the Geist is cool to have the Sin-Eater in control of the reigns, when it drops they are getting more restless and agitated until it's Synergy 0 and they make the Sin-Eater their meat puppet... Things get too crunchy otherwise, the system would work more at low Synergy when a contest of wills would come in.<br /> <br /> I'm more a favour of the one bar... I picture the Geist pushing more mental antagonism onto the Sin-Eater as it drops, which is equivalent to the Conditions of a dropped Integrity being placed upon them... Rather than the Sin-Eater kicking themselves or reacting badly to their Breaking Points, the Geist is doing it. Like I said in the other thread, I see Synergy more as a measure of the patience the Geist has with the Sin-Eater they're bonded to than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T06:16:01-07:00","id":270760,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about this and - considering the directions of GMC - I'm thinking there's a far simpler answer that involves making the players do the extra work rather than the ST.<br /> <br /> Firstly, my interpretation of Synergy is that it's a more passive score: it represents the health of the bond you have with a Geist who is attempting to be essentially your subconscious personality. Basically, a high synergy score represents to what amounts to one mind: although your Geist might disagree with your choices, it'd never truly override them because you take the perspective of the rational mind.A low Synergy score to contrast would be about the equivalent of a person with multiple splintered personalities- two minds that share the bare minimum amount of ground and contradict eachother, with the Geist even sometimes taking control.<br /> <br /> That's why I'm gonna suggest you use conditions rather than a direct contest of wills.<br /> <br /> To use an example that I really like that's on the boards, lets use a Geist that gets caught up in the thrill of the hunt. During play, the Sin Eaters come across a dangerous predator than the ST might apply the following condition:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bloodlust<br /> <br /> Your character is titillated by the idea of hunting worthy game. You take a -2 to mental rolls unrelated to tracking, hunting or killing of this prey.<br /> <br /> Beat: gain a beat whenever you make significant progress in hunting and killing the target.<br /> <br /> Resolution: this condition is resolved when the target is either killed or no longer seen as worthy game. Gain a beat if you resolve this condition by killing the target. This condition can also be removed with 24 hours of rest and meditation. </div> </div> </div>Just a thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}